---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How DayAlmanac handles visitor data, advertising cookies, and your choices."
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px]">
		<h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--ink)] md:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--ink)]/40">Last updated: July 31, 2026</p>

		<div class="prose-content mt-7 max-w-[640px] text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.85] text-[var(--ink)]/70">
			<p>
				DayAlmanac ("DayAlmanac," "we," "us," or "our") operates dayalmanac.com (the "Site"). This
				Privacy Policy explains what information is collected when you visit the Site, how it's
				used, and the choices you have. By using the Site, you agree to the practices described
				here.
			</p>

			<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
			<p>
				DayAlmanac does not require you to create an account, submit a form, or leave a comment to
				use the Site, and we do not directly collect personal information such as your name, email
				address, or payment details.
			</p>
			<p>We do collect limited information automatically, through:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Basic access logs and analytics.</strong> Our hosting provider (Cloudflare)
					automatically logs standard technical data for every visit, such as IP address, browser
					type, device type, referring page, and pages viewed. This is used in aggregate to
					understand traffic and keep the Site running reliably, not to identify individual
					visitors.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Advertising cookies from third parties.</strong> As the Site grows, we plan to
					display ads served by advertising partners (such as Google AdSense and, potentially,
					Mediavine, AdThrive, or Ezoic). These companies use cookies and similar technologies to
					serve ads, including personalized ads based on your visits to this and other websites,
					and to measure ad performance. See Section 4 for details and your choices.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
			<p>The limited data described above is used to:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Operate, maintain, and secure the Site</li>
				<li>Understand aggregate traffic patterns and which content is useful to readers</li>
				<li>Allow our advertising partners to serve and measure ads, which is how DayAlmanac is funded</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				We do not sell personal information, and we do not use the data we have direct access to
				(aggregate traffic logs) to build individual profiles of visitors.
			</p>

			<h2>3. Legal Basis for Processing (EU/UK Visitors)</h2>
			<p>
				If you are located in the European Economic Area or the UK, our legal basis for the limited
				processing described above is our legitimate interest in operating and funding the Site
				through advertising, and, for non-essential cookies (including advertising cookies), your
				consent, which you can withdraw at any time using the cookie controls described in Section 4.
			</p>

			<h2>4. Cookies and Advertising</h2>
			<p><strong>What cookies are used for.</strong> Advertising networks we work with place cookies in your browser to:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Serve ads, including ads personalized to your interests based on browsing activity</li>
				<li>Limit how many times you see the same ad</li>
				<li>Measure the effectiveness of ad campaigns</li>
				<li>Detect and prevent fraudulent activity</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your
				visit to this Site and/or other sites on the internet. Google's own data practices for
				advertising are described in its
				<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Business Data Responsibilities policy</a>
				and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy &amp; Terms</a>.
			</p>
			<p><strong>Your choices.</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li>You can opt out of personalized advertising by Google by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
				<li>If you're outside the US, you can also visit <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info/choices</a> or, in the EU, <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">youronlinechoices.eu</a> to opt out of participating vendors' personalized advertising.</li>
				<li>Most browsers let you block or delete cookies in their settings. Blocking cookies may still allow ads to display, just without personalization.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>5. Third-Party Advertising Partners</h2>
			<p>
				As the Site grows, we plan to work with advertising partners such as Google AdSense, and
				potentially Mediavine, AdThrive, or Ezoic. Any partner we add will have its own privacy
				policy governing how it uses data collected through its ads, and we will update this policy
				to reflect new partners as they're added.
			</p>

			<h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
			<p>
				Aggregate server/access logs are retained only as long as needed for security and
				operational purposes, per our hosting provider's standard retention practices. We do not
				maintain a separate database of visitor information beyond this.
			</p>

			<h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
			<p>
				Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or receive a
				copy of personal information relating to you, and to object to or restrict certain
				processing (this includes rights under the GDPR for EU/UK residents and the CCPA/CPRA for
				California residents). Because DayAlmanac does not maintain accounts or collect personal
				information directly, most of these requests will concern data held by our advertising
				partners (see Section 4 for opt-out links) rather than data held by us. If you have a
				question about data practices specific to this Site, you can contact us using the details
				in Section 10.
			</p>
			<p>
				California residents: we do not sell personal information as defined under the CCPA/CPRA.
				Some cookie-based advertising may be considered "sharing" for cross-context behavioral
				advertising under California law; you can opt out using the tools listed in Section 4.
			</p>

			<h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
			<p>
				DayAlmanac is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
				information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us with personal
				information, contact us and we will address it.
			</p>

			<h2>9. International Visitors</h2>
			<p>
				The Site is hosted and operated with a US audience primarily in mind, but is accessible
				globally. If you access the Site from outside the United States, your information (to the
				limited extent described above) may be processed in the United States or other countries
				where our service providers operate.
			</p>

			<h2>10. Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about this Privacy Policy can be sent to Owen Zhang via the contact information
				listed on the Site's <a href="/about/">About</a> page.
			</p>

			<h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
			<p>
				We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time, for example as we add new advertising
				partners. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page reflects the most recent
				revision. Continued use of the Site after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the
				updated policy.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.prose-content :global(h2) {
		margin-top: 1.75rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
		color: var(--ink);
	}
	.prose-content :global(h2:first-child) {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.prose-content :global(p) {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.prose-content :global(ul) {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
		list-style: disc;
	}
	.prose-content :global(li) {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	.prose-content :global(a) {
		color: var(--flag-dark);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
</style>
